      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "## Nexus-7 Optical Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n### 1. Product Overview\n*   **Device Identification:** Nexus-7 Optical Proximity Sensor.\n*   **Core Functionality:** Measures distance via optical sensing.\n\n### 2. Electrical Specifications\n*   **Power Requirements:** Operates on a stable DC voltage range of 3.3V to 5V.\n*   **Pin Configuration:** Utilizes a standard 4-pin header for connectivity.\n    *   VCC (Power Input)\n    *   GND (Ground Reference)\n    *   OUT (Analog Signal Output)\n    *   Enable (Control Signal)\n\n### 3. Operational Parameters\n*   **Sensing Range:** The sensor reliably detects objects between 2cm and 40cm.\n*   **Output Signal:** Provides an analog voltage output directly proportional to the measured distance.\n\n### 4. Deployment and Safety Protocols\n*   **Pre-Deployment Requirement:** Calibration must be executed in a strictly stable environmental setting prior to field use.\n*   **Environmental Warnings:** Critical operational constraints include avoiding direct exposure to sunlight and preventing moisture ingress.",
